2. Never allow more than six guests per treehouse.
3. Never allocate more bunkbeds than available.
4. Prevent overlapping active treehouse bookings.
5. Prevent negative guest counts and payment amounts.
6. Validate all discounts before saving.
7. Validate food quantities.
8. Handle simultaneous booking attempts safely.
9. Confirm payment changes on the backend.
10. Use secure server-side calculations for final booking totals.
11. Preserve existing records during pricing updates.
12. Validate user permissions before every sensitive operation.
13. Prevent direct database access from bypassing role permissions.
14. Store all timestamps consistently and display dates in the Asia/Kolkata timezone.

Use transaction-safe reservation writes.

The app should be reliable even when multiple team members are booking at the same time.

